From: Yury Klushin <digger@live.ru>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:36:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] pdp11: zero .bss in the rt11 crt0 before touching statics

RT-11 doesn't clear memory between programs, so a previous job's
leftovers can still be sitting in a freshly loaded program's .bss --
including this crt0's own cmdbuf/argv buffers, which are declared
there. Add a zero-fill loop over __bss_start..._end (from the linker
script, ld/scripttempl/pdp11rt11.sc in the wdigger/binutils-gdb fork)
right after the SP is set from the SAV header, before anything else
touches memory.

Verified via SIMH: reads/writes cleanly and reaches the program's own
halt without crashing; a global array poked with nonzero data before
the fixed crt0 runs reads back as zero once main is reached.

Includes what was a separate fix on top of this one, now part of it:

pdp11: crt0rt: clear .bss with an unsigned compare

The loop that clears .bss ended on BGE, a signed compare of two
addresses.  A .bss that starts below 0100000 (32 KB) and ends above it
then compares as start >= end, and is not cleared at all: a program of
more than 32 KB starts with whatever was in that memory.  BHIS compares
them unsigned.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libgcc/config/pdp11/crt0rt.s | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libgcc/config/pdp11/crt0rt.s b/libgcc/config/pdp11/crt0rt.s
index 81b25f5..7a9e6c9 100644
--- a/libgcc/config/pdp11/crt0rt.s
+++ b/libgcc/config/pdp11/crt0rt.s
@@ -12,6 +12,21 @@ cmdbuf_max = 80
 start:
         mov   @$042, sp   // SP comes from the SAV header (RT-11 sets it before we start)
 
+        // RT-11 doesn't clear memory between programs, so a previous job's
+        // leftovers can still be sitting in our .bss; zero it before touching
+        // any of our own statics (including cmdbuf/argv below).  __bss_start
+        // and _end come from the linker script (ld/scripttempl/pdp11rt11.sc).
+        mov   $__bss_start, r1
+        mov   $_end, r2
+        // Addresses are unsigned: BHIS, not BGE.  With BGE a .bss that
+        // straddles 0100000 (32 KB) -- start below, end above -- compares
+        // as start >= end and is left uncleared.
+4$:     cmp   r1, r2
+        bhis  5$
+        clrb  (r1)+
+        br    4$
+5$:
+
         // RT-11's KMON, when it runs a program via RUN (or by typing its name
         // directly), copies whatever followed the program name on that command
         // into the fixed "chain area": a byte count at address 0510 and the
-- 
